1) Rumor has it you can do the task yourself if you are polymorphed
into the one class of monsters in the dungeon with "unlimited"
carrying capacity which you are able to become.

2) If you put everything you want Phideaux to carry into a blessed bag
of holding, and his Rexiness is very well trained at playing fetch,
it is the next best thing to having a pack beast, especially when
combined with a magic whistle.

3) Speaking of which, several pets can share the workload, with the
odds being better that at least one of them picks stuff up and you
can whistle it your way as part of a mob.

4) Otherwise, yes, but you won't really like the results. Put the
stuff you want carried into an expendable bag, let your pet
gelatinous cube eat the bag, thus making the undamaged goods its
"guts"; summon it after you with the whistle, and "accidentally"
cause its death at the destination, unpacking The Luggage as it
were.

That may waste time, infuriate your deity, expose you to attack
easily from other monsters, guarantee that every nymph or
leprechaun in earshot is awake, and otherwise be worse than making
many trips yourself, plus the dumb beast might fall through a trap
and end up several levels misplaced, or similarly onto a level
transporter and be some unknown elsewhere.

I told you you wouldn't like it!  ;-)

You may prefer researching the rather high risk methods of
putting one blessed bag of holding inside another one without
blowing them both up, to cut your burden to 16th what you are
carrying instead of 1/4th.

Or, as another option, check yourself into a "packrat
deprogramming" or "clutter co-dependence" clinic.

xanthian, the best ascension is the first one, I've been
told; I wouldn't know.

There are probably lots of disasters I forgot. Can a G-cube
set itself on fire in a magic trap, for example?


